### W52 · Context across sessions

A codebase audit will span about three sessions. Each new session re-explores modules the
previous one already covered, because nothing from earlier sessions survives. Best
approach?

A) Resume the previous session each day so earlier exploration is still in context.
B) Run one long session and `/compact` whenever it nears the context limit.
C) Keep a findings file the agent updates as it works and reads at each session start.
D) Append each day's findings to the project `CLAUDE.md` so every session loads them.

